From 1f754f8c06dc2ae1e48b8dd6b7dd244904a4acfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Khai Wen, Ng" <khai.wen.ng@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 09:05:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/47] maxim-serdes: max_des: Use stream_id instead of routing
 stream

max9296a has needs_unique_stream_id, which means using stream_id
from routing will not work. Only use route->sink_stream for
max96724 which does not requires unique_stream_id.

Tested-on: maxim-serdes with 2x isx031 on single max9296 on ARL.

Signed-off-by: Khai Wen, Ng <khai.wen.ng@intel.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
index af64576c3bdf..017950c254ef 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
@@ -1522,7 +1522,12 @@ static int max_des_update_pipe_enable(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 		}
 
 		if (des->ops->set_pipe_stream_id) {
-			pipe->stream_id = route->sink_stream;
+			/* Use sink stream from routing if deserializer does not
+			 * need unique stream id, i.e. max96724
+			 */
+			if (!des->ops->needs_unique_stream_id)
+				pipe->stream_id = route->sink_stream;
+
 			ret = des->ops->set_pipe_stream_id(des, pipe,
 							   pipe->stream_id);
 			if (ret)
-- 
2.34.1

